An opt-in `--heap-free-lambda-facts` option checks a lambda without a reads clause, whose body observes neither the heap nor allocation, in every good heap without assuming its parameters allocated, and then permits the calls in its body to unfold wherever the lambda is applied. This restores, for such lambdas, facts that the finite-support and function-value allocation repairs had guarded: for example `(a: int) => 7 - Idx(a)` is again an `int -> nat`, and a family `(o: nat -> int) => F(o)` unfolds at a quantified `o`.
